<title>TURKEY: Turkish central bank reserve rises last week.</title>
<headline>Turkish central bank reserve rises last week.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Friday its foreign currency reserve rose by $205 million to $16.864 billion in the week ending February 7.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollar</p>
<p>			  February 7   January 31    End-1996</p>
<p> Forex reserve	  16.864	 16.659	16.491</p>
<p> Gold reserve	    1.383	  1.383	 1.383</p>
<p> Total reserve	  18.247	 18.042	17.784</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, fell by $118 million to $26.759 billion in the week ending January 24, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
